codex
I found the likely root cause: on the ready-assert cycle, the wrapper can clear hold and allow core request turnover in the same cycle, which can cause a second request/commit before commit accounting catches up. I’ll make a single-line stall-tightening fix so the core only advances after the held request is fully drained.
apply patch
patch: completed
